            <ArticleTitle>Saphenous nerve entrapment. A cause of medial knee pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>80-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Saphenous nerve entrapment is a seldom recognized cause of pain along the medial side of the knee and proximal calf. We are reporting our experience with 15 saphenous nerve entrapments in 14 patients between 1978 and 1981.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
